course: dictionary
lesson: 11320
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words look the same but mean different things, and you find the right meaning by reading the words around them. Yi is one of these words. It is not an English word, so you might meet it in a Chinese number lesson, in a geography book, or as a name.
explain: In a Chinese number lesson, yī means "one" and sounds like English "ee". The numbers go yī, èr, sān: one, two, three. In geography, the Yi are a people of south-west China with their own language and script. The lesson or subject around the word tells you which meaning to use.
explain: «Among the major Cyrillic alphabets, the letter "ї" (sounds like "yi", as in "Україна") is used only in Ukrainian and the closely related Rusyn.» Here yi describes a sound, not a meaning. Always ask what the words around it are about, then put your meaning into the sentence to check that it fits.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Yī» is Mandarin Chinese for "one", and it sounds like English "ee".
fact: The Yi are an ethnic group in south-west China, with their own Yi language and script.
fact: Yi is also a common Korean and Chinese surname, also written Lee or Li, as in Admiral Yi Sun-sin of Korea.
fact: Yi is not an English word, so the lesson around it is your best clue.
exercise: In a Chinese number lesson, «yī, èr, sān» are the first three numbers. What does yī mean? | *One | Three | Two
exercise: The Yi are a people. Where do they live? | Europe | Africa | *South-west China | Korea
exercise: Yi is also a surname, as in Admiral Yi Sun-sin of Korea. Which other spelling of this surname is given? | Brown | *Lee | Patel
test: In «the Yi people», what kind of word is Yi? | A verb | *A proper noun, the name of a people | A number | An adjective
test: The letter «ї» sounds like "yi" in «Україна». Which language uses this letter? | Chinese | English | Korean | *Ukrainian
exam: Jayden sees «yi» in a maths book, beside «èr» and «sān». What does it most likely mean? | Yes | Blue | Four | *One
